WEBVTT

q0001
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:08.257
What goes wrong when one method name is used as the answer to three different questions?

q0002
00:00:08.257 --> 00:00:17.397
This episode has one job: CM is not automatically a compact representation, a satisfiability solver, CM-IR, or a universally fastest execution method.

q0003
00:00:17.397 --> 00:00:26.537
We build on What a correspondence matrix is; their definitions stay fixed while this lesson adds a new layer.

q0004
00:00:26.537 --> 00:00:33.331
A representation or solver is defined partly by the output contract it satisfies.

q0005
00:00:33.331 --> 00:00:41.588
Watch for the label complete truth layout; it stays attached to the artifact this episode means.

q0006
00:00:41.588 --> 00:00:48.870
When we say satisfiability question, the highlight identifies its layer before we interpret it.

q0007
00:00:48.870 --> 00:00:58.010
The term universal performance claim receives its own visual state so it cannot drift into a neighboring concept.

q0008
00:00:58.010 --> 00:01:06.754
The next sequence uses Four-variable truth layout as a conceptual teaching example, not as measured benchmark evidence.

q0009
00:01:06.754 --> 00:01:10.623
Our stable example is Four-variable truth layout.

q0010
00:01:10.623 --> 00:01:19.763
F(A,B,C,D)=(A AND B) XOR (C OR D), row variables A,B, column variables C,D, MSB-first ordering.

q0011
00:01:19.763 --> 00:01:27.045
Carry assignments, live support, explicit CM, packed truth vectors, and exact output across episodes.

q0012
00:01:27.045 --> 00:01:34.327
We now construct the Four-variable truth layout and name every part before interpreting it.

q0013
00:01:34.327 --> 00:01:43.467
Ask for a complete vector, one satisfying assignment, and a reusable program, then show the different output each task requires.

q0014
00:01:43.467 --> 00:01:50.749
Pair a scoped kernel result with the slower public wrapper to reject method-label reasoning.

q0015
00:01:50.749 --> 00:01:55.106
Now isolate CM non-claims inside Four-variable truth layout.

q0016
00:01:55.106 --> 00:02:03.363
The example definition and output meaning stay fixed while only the state for CM non-claims changes.

q0017
00:02:03.363 --> 00:02:11.620
That matched before-and-after view assigns the visible consequence to CM non-claims, not to a substituted workload.

q0018
00:02:11.620 --> 00:02:19.877
A dense grid, SAT witness, and CM-IR DAG are aligned by requested output rather than ranked.

q0019
00:02:19.877 --> 00:02:24.721
Now isolate output-contract mismatch examples inside Four-variable truth layout.

q0020
00:02:24.721 --> 00:02:33.465
The example definition and output meaning stay fixed while only the state for output-contract mismatch examples changes.

q0021
00:02:33.465 --> 00:02:42.209
That matched before-and-after view assigns the visible consequence to output-contract mismatch examples, not to a substituted workload.

q0022
00:02:42.209 --> 00:02:51.349
CM, CM-IR, SAT, BDD, minimization, and symbolic algebra answer different questions and must be compared under matched output contracts.

q0023
00:02:51.349 --> 00:02:57.656
Read that statement only within this scope: implemented backend and task contracts.

q0024
00:02:57.656 --> 00:03:01.525
Its declared measurement boundary is output contract.

q0025
00:03:01.525 --> 00:03:04.907
The uncertainty field says scope dependent.

q0026
00:03:04.907 --> 00:03:13.164
An explicit dense CM and CM-IR are different artifacts with different construction, storage, and evaluation boundaries.

q0027
00:03:13.164 --> 00:03:18.008
Read that statement only within this scope: current implementation.

q0028
00:03:18.008 --> 00:03:22.365
Its declared measurement boundary is representation and evaluation.

q0029
00:03:22.365 --> 00:03:25.259
The uncertainty field says none.

q0030
00:03:25.259 --> 00:03:31.566
Current evidence does not support a universal claim that CM beats CSE-flat.

q0031
00:03:31.566 --> 00:03:36.410
Read that statement only within this scope: cross-study synthesis.

q0032
00:03:36.410 --> 00:03:41.254
Its declared measurement boundary is multiple boundaries kept separate.

q0033
00:03:41.254 --> 00:03:46.098
The uncertainty field says scopes are intentionally not pooled.

q0034
00:03:46.098 --> 00:03:55.238
The nearest confusing lesson is Explicit dense CM versus CM-IR; it owns dense CM versus CM-IR artifact distinction, while this episode owns CM non-claims.

q0035
00:03:55.238 --> 00:04:04.378
The example fixes F of A, B, C, and D as A AND B, exclusive-or C OR D.

q0036
00:04:04.378 --> 00:04:09.710
Holding that element fixed lets this episode isolate CM non-claims.

q0037
00:04:09.710 --> 00:04:18.850
A and B select the row, C and D select the column, and MSB-first order fixes both index conventions.

q0038
00:04:18.850 --> 00:04:24.669
Holding that element fixed lets this episode isolate output-contract mismatch examples.

q0039
00:04:24.669 --> 00:04:33.809
Every four-bit assignment names exactly one of the sixteen cells, and every cell returns one exact output bit.

q0040
00:04:33.809 --> 00:04:41.578
Folding the truth-table output column into a four-by-four grid changes the layout, not the function.

q0041
00:04:41.578 --> 00:04:50.718
Reading a cell forward evaluates an assignment; reading it backward recovers the row and column bits that selected it.

q0042
00:04:50.718 --> 00:04:59.858
Live support can remove an input from active computation even when the ambient layout still reserves its axis.

q0043
00:04:59.858 --> 00:05:08.998
A packed truth vector stores the same exact outputs in a different physical arrangement from the displayed matrix.

q0044
00:05:08.998 --> 00:05:16.767
Current evidence supports scoped comparisons, not a claim that CM wins every task or boundary.

q0045
00:05:16.767 --> 00:05:22.586
Match matrix, program graph, and SAT witness to three output requests.

q0046
00:05:22.586 --> 00:05:28.405
CM is one exact representation family, not a universal answer label.

q0047
00:05:28.405 --> 00:05:36.174
A common mistake is this: Calling an approach CM establishes compactness, solver behavior, or speed.

q0048
00:05:36.174 --> 00:05:41.506
Repair it by returning to the owned distinction: CM non-claims.

q0050
00:05:44.553 --> 00:05:53.693
Use the episode's central distinction to answer: CM is one exact representation family, not a universal answer label.

q0051
00:05:53.693 --> 00:06:00.000
Ask what must be returned before asking which method should return it.
